---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { correctionsEmail } from "../lib/contact.ts";

export const prerender = true;
const email = correctionsEmail(Astro);
---

<Base title="Privacy | Golf Outing Finder" description="What Golf Outing Finder collects and why: no accounts, no tracking of your location, and ads only with consent where required." path="/privacy" noindex crumbs={[{ name: "Privacy", path: "/privacy" }]}>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>Golf Outing Finder has no accounts and no sign-up. Here is what happens when you use it.</p>
  <h2>Your location</h2>
  <p>
    If you press "Use my location", your browser asks for permission and sends your approximate position to our server only to
    find nearby outings. We don't store it or log it.
  </p>
  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>Our hosting provider sees IP addresses to deliver pages and stop abuse. We use them only for short-lived rate limiting.</p>
  <h2>Analytics and ads</h2>
  <p>
    The site is free because of display ads. Listing pages and outing pages show ads from Google AdSense (or another ad network
    we may switch to), and we may use Google Analytics to count visits and see which pages people use. Ads appear in boxes
    marked "Advertisement"; we never sell a better spot in a list.
  </p>
  <p>
    These services can set cookies and use similar storage in your browser: advertising cookies that help choose and measure
    ads and limit how often you see the same one, and analytics cookies that tell one visit from the next. Google uses this
    information as described in
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use
    our services</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    We use Google Consent Mode. If you're in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, ad and analytics
    cookies are off until you choose in the consent message, which Google's consent tool shows on your first visit. Until you
    agree, ads can still appear but aren't personalized, and no analytics cookies are set. Elsewhere, these cookies are on by
    default.
  </p>
  <h2>Changing your choice</h2>
  <p>
    Where the consent message applies, use the "Privacy choices" link in the footer of any listing or outing page to open it
    again and change your answer. You can also clear or block cookies in your browser settings, and turn off personalized ads
    from Google at <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/">My Ad Center</a>.
  </p>
  <h2>Links to organizers</h2>
  <p>Register buttons take you to the organizer's or a registration platform's site, which has its own privacy policy.</p>
  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
</Base>
